body: "The spec requires exact use-site bindings in native glossary state. The current package stores senses, aliases and replay in the native owner, and reserves an empty collection for bindings.\n\n> All authoritative glossary state and exact use-site bindings live in SDK custom fields and native history with no side files or Git runtime requirement\n\n`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `README.md`, and PR #1 document the deferral. The `docs/real-data.md` records zero bindings. The package already tracks the implementation as `pm-glossary-3jep`.\n\nAdd an authorized native binding operation with immutable source revision and exact UTF-8 span evidence. Cover concurrent binds, stale revisions, changed/absent/inaccessible sources, and replay without duplicate history. Verify that the CLI and SDK share the binding contract and work in a plain tracker."
